# Gateway & Codex integration

## Services

- `GatewayServer` — HTTP routing on `127.0.0.1:8765`, third-party model proxy, OpenAI pass-through. Anthropic Console (`auth_kind: anthropic`) and Claude Code login (`auth_kind: claude_code`) both use `https://api.anthropic.com/v1` OpenAI-compat `/chat/completions` and `/models`; Claude Code tokens come from `ClaudeCodeSession` at request time (never stored). Custom routing: `ModelCatalog.requestedModelID` + unique unprefixed `findModel`. Pass-through: `passthroughAuthorization` replaces dummy/`not-used`/missing bearer with `~/.codex/auth.json` (or drops the header when no token is available); ChatGPT `auth_mode` + `tokens.account_id` uses `chatgpt.com/backend-api/codex` (not `api.openai.com`). `ResponsesStreamState` emits `function_call` events. TLS is system trust (with or without Zscaler).
- `LoopbackHTTPServer` — Network.framework HTTP server, SSE support.
- `Translator` — Responses ↔ Chat Completions translation, namespace tool mapping, think-block stripping.
- `ModelCatalog` — `~/.codexgateway/custom_model_catalog.json` + `providers.json`. Picker export `~/.codex/model-catalogs/custom-providers.json` is custom models only. `isNativeCodexSlug` is the built-in GPT-5 set plus cached `codex debug models --bundled` slugs (5s timeout); those slugs are not aliased onto a custom model. Exact catalog slugs such as `cursor/gpt-5.5` still match first.
- `CodexConfig` — managed blocks in `~/.codex/config.toml` (markers `# >>> codexgateway managed >>>`). `requires_openai_auth` on the `codexgateway` provider is derived from `isSignedIn()` (auth.json): `false` when signed out so Codex skips login for local-only Ollama/custom use; `true` when signed in. The picker export stays custom models only; ChatGPT rejects native Codex model ids on the gateway path. Legacy `codexbar` blocks are rewritten to `codexgateway` on refresh/patch. Automatic callers (startup, auth watcher, restart) use `refreshManagedConfigIfApplied()` — they only re-patch when the block already exists, never injecting into a native Codex. Explicit apply is `patchCodexConfig()` via `SettingsStore.updateGatewayConfig` / add-model/provider actions.
- `CodexAuthWatcher` — watches `~/.codex` for sign-in changes and re-patches config automatically; `restartCodexDesktop()` also re-patches before relaunch.
- `CodexAppServer` — locate Codex binary. `restartCodexDesktop()` restarts the Codex app and `CodexCLIDaemon` (`codex app-server daemon restart`).

## Config paths

- `Paths.modelCatalog`, `Paths.providersConfig`, `Paths.codexConfig`, `Paths.codexAuth`
- Gateway: `Paths.gatewayHost`:`Paths.gatewayPort` (default `127.0.0.1:8765`)

## After changing these services

Run `make test` and update `ARCHITECTURE.md`, `README.md` (if user-visible), and this rule or `codexgateway-gateway` skill when integration contracts change.

## Do not

- Duplicate HTTP routing logic outside `GatewayServer`.
- Write to `~/.codex/config.toml` outside `CodexConfig` managed blocks without good reason.
- Re-enable WebSocket/voice endpoints without explicit user request.
